  "question": {
    "text": "If the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, is the tangent to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the vertex of the parabola, then the slope of the line through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is"
  },
